# UI changes — edit only

When changing UI (layout, styling, components, pages, client state, or rendered data), make the code change and stop.

- Do not start, restart, or check a dev server (`npm run dev`, `npm run local:dev`, or any other server).
- Do not open a browser, use browser tools, take screenshots, or click through the app to verify the change.
- Do not run curl, rendering scripts, or other substitutes to preview the UI.

```text
❌ BAD — after a styling edit
Start the dev server, open /dashboard, and screenshot the page.

✅ GOOD — after a styling edit
Update the component and report what changed.
```

The same limit applies to logic and API changes. Do not run tests, typecheck, lint, or a build unless the user asks. See `do-not-test-until-asked.mdc`.
